      "text": "To solve for the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\), we first need to find the roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\). Let the roots be \\(r, s, t\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\n1. \\(r + s + t = 5\\)\n2. \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\)\n3. \\(rst = 9\\)\n\nWe want to compute the expression \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). Starting from:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\n\\]\n\n we can group the terms as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs}{rst} + \\frac{st \\cdot ts}{rst} + \\frac{tr \\cdot rt}{rst} = \\frac{r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2}{rst}\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(rst = 9\\), this expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2}{9}\n\\]\n\nWe know from Vieta's formulas that \\(r + s + t = 5\\). Squaring both sides gives:\n\n\\[\nr^2 + s^2 + t^2 + 2(rs + rt + st) = 25\n\\]\n\nSince \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\), substituting this, we get:\n\n\\[\nr^2 + s^2 + t^2 + 2 \\cdot 6 = 25 \\implies r^2 + s^2 + t^2 = 25 - 12 = 13\n\\]\n\nNow, using the identity \\(r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t)\\), we substitute the known values:\n\n\\[\n(r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2}{9} = \\frac{-54}{9} = -6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}\n\\]",
